# Methodology (read before any analysis or modelling)

## Core quantity
Daily performance index is the irradiance-normalized yield:

    PI = daily_total_production / daily_irradiation

This proxies system efficiency. Soiling shows up as a downward drift of PI
between two consecutive panel washes, and a step-up recovery right after a wash.

## Temperature correction (preferred PR)
Module power has temperature coefficient -0.35 %/degC referenced to 25 degC
cell temperature (Jinko JKM525-545M datasheet). When ambient temperature is
available (NASA POWER), estimate cell temp with the NOCT model
(NOCT = 45 degC) and correct PI to 25 degC before fitting soiling slopes.
Report both raw PI and temperature-corrected PI.

## Mandatory confounder removal before fitting soiling
Exclude or flag days that are not "clean efficiency" observations:
- Days overlapping any downtime in the downtime log, especially
  Kisitlama (curtailment), Plansiz/Planli Calisma, Ariza, Yillik Bakim.
- Very low irradiance days (clouds) below a configurable threshold.
- Rain days: rainfall is natural washing; model it as a separate recovery term,
  do not confuse it with soiling drift.
Log how many days each filter drops.

## Washing segments
The washing-dates file defines segments. Two washing methods appear
(brush+solution vs robot no-solution). For each inter-wash segment fit a
soiling-rate model (PI vs days-since-wash); compare rate and recovery across
seasons and washing methods.

## From soiling rate to schedule (the actual deliverable)
Translate the fitted soiling rate into an economic optimum washing interval:
cumulative soiling energy loss vs washing cost. Optimal interval minimizes
total cost per MWh. Washing cost and electricity price are external inputs;
if absent, request them and meanwhile run a sensitivity sweep over plausible
ranges. State every assumption in the report.

## Machine learning role
Random Forest (and GridSearchCV) is the SECONDARY layer required by the
proposal: predict daily PI or soiling rate from weather features
(temp, wind, rainfall, dust/PM10, days-since-wash, season). Report MAE, RMSE, R2
with a TIME-BASED train/test split (never random shuffle on a time series) and
feature importances. The physical/statistical soiling model above is the primary,
defensible result; ML supports it, it does not replace it.

## Scope note
Project proposal compares Canakkale (polluted) vs Balikesir (clean). Only
